[
  {"lesson": "m-eurosat (2000 train images, 64px, 13 bands): ResNet50 with ssl4eo_s2 weights upsampled to 128px scored 0.986 in a 1.5-min screen and 0.985 over 30 epochs. The 64px ssl4eo_s2 variants scored 0.973-0.979 in the same screen. Upsampling is a cheap way to get more from pretrained filters on small Sentinel-2 chips. It was run once (one change from the 64px baseline), so treat it as indicative.", "tags": ["sentinel-2", "classification", "m-eurosat", "img_size"]},
  {"lesson": "On m-eurosat, ssl4eo_s2 weights clearly beat imagenet weights with the same ResNet50 config at 64px: 0.979 vs 0.946 in the rung-1 screen (1.5 min). Use ssl4eo_s2 on Sentinel-2 tasks, and don't spend budget on imagenet there.", "tags": ["sentinel-2", "classification", "m-eurosat", "weights"]},
  {"lesson": "m-eurosat training is cheap: ResNet50 at 64px takes about 0.04 min/epoch and at 128px about 0.065 min/epoch. A full 30-epoch run takes about 2 min, so a 6-config halving round with 1.5-min screens finished 6 trials in about 9 min with no epoch warnings. Short screens are enough on small datasets, and the saved budget can go to seed checks.", "tags": ["sentinel-2", "classification", "m-eurosat", "budget"]},
  {"lesson": "Seed noise on m-eurosat validation (1000 images) is about ±0.002: five seeds of the same config scored 0.983-0.988, mean 0.9856. A 3-model ensemble (0.989) and TTA (0.987-0.988) tied with the best single seed (0.988), so they gave no gain beyond noise. Differences under 0.003 between configs should be treated as ties.", "tags": ["sentinel-2", "classification", "m-eurosat", "seed-noise", "ensemble"]}
]
